From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] twinapi.appcore: Windows.System.Profile.SystemIdentification gives a stable machine identifier

Windows.System.Profile.SystemIdentification was missing: activating it
failed with REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG. AnyDesk's service asks for it to know
the machine again ("Could not get system ID (0x80040154)" in
ad_svc.trace at every start, and again at every device-ID update);
David's installed AnyDesk came up with a different address after
restarts.

GetSystemIdForPublisher and GetSystemIdForUser now give a 32-byte
identifier that is the same on every call and after every restart, and
different on every other machine: a SHA-256 hash of the machine's
MachineGuid (HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Cryptography, made once with the
machine's Windows side) and what it is for -- the publisher (a desktop
program has no package, so all share one) or the calling user's SID.
Its Source is SystemIdentificationSource.Registry. The Id is a
Windows.Storage.Streams.Buffer.

Test: test/sysid-gate.sh with test/sysid-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_NO_SYSTEM_ID).
